The card's boot script expects one of these, and says which at boot.
If it names a different one, the lease moved and this is the fix:
            StarFive # setenv nife_boot_server 192.168.8.192

For a UEFI client (xenon, milestone 260) the same address goes in the router's
dhcp-boot line; see bench/xenon-netboot/dnsmasq.conf. There is no prompt to fix it at.

